    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34596" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pēra</span></b> , ae, f., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πἠρα</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a bag</i>, <i>wallet</i>
			(syn.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mantica, loculus): peras imposuit Juppiter
					nobis duas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Phaedr. 4, 10, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cum baculo perāque senex, of a Cynic
					philosopher,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					4, 53, 3</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">App. Mag. p. 287, 39</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Vulg.
				1 Reg. 17, 40</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Luc. 10, 4</span></i>.</div>
